+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The uu-grep executable checks pledge before processing arguments or input.
It permits stdio, rpath and tty for input files, localization, output and
terminal detection. It cannot start programs, open ordinary files for
writing or create network connections after that call.

There is no unveil policy: recursive and user-selected paths remain readable
under the user's normal permissions. Stdio also permits I/O on inherited
descriptors. This is a syscall boundary, not complete filesystem or network
isolation. The embedding Rust library does not change the caller's policy.

The port requires the current OpenBSD Rust package, whose current_exe()
implementation uses getexecpath(). Older Rust implementations may require
additional system calls and have not been validated with this policy.

Native validation of locale/help output, terminals, SIGPIPE, input paths and
denied operations is still required. No native runtime guarantee is claimed.
